This is code used for computing matchings and finding (suboptimal) solutions to the reference problem.

The project should be located in the same directory containing sonLib (https://github.com/benedictpaten/sonLib), which must be installed.
Given this requirement a simple 'make all' should be enough to build the project. 'make test' will then do a batch of obligatory tests.

The matching algorithms are in inc/stMatchingAlgorithms.h. chooseMatching_edmonds computes an exact maximum weight
matching in process, with a C translation of Joris van Rantwijk's MIT licensed implementation of Edmonds' blossom
algorithm; it replaces the Blossom V program (blossom5), which this project used to bundle but whose license does not
allow redistribution. chooseMatching_maximumWeightMatching and chooseMatching_maximumCardinalityMatching run
externalTools/matchGraph/matchGraph.py instead.

The code is released under the MIT license, see LICENSE.txt.
